Class: FlightRecord
Responsibilities:

- Store the current state of a single tracked aircraft (callsign, type, position, altitude, speed, heading, and last-seen time)
- Update individual fields when a newer decoded packet arrives
- Provide a snapshot of all current flight data on request
- Track the history of recent positions for trend analysis

Collaborators (if any):
- AircraftDatabase
- SafetyAnalyzer

Assumptions (if any):
- One FlightRecord exists per active aircraft in the system
- Record is removed or archived if no update is received within a configurable timeout

Class: AircraftDatabase
- Store and index all active FlightRecords, keyed by aircraft identifier
- Insert a new FlightRecord when an unknown aircraft is first detected
- Update an existing FlightRecord with the latest decoded data
- Retrieve a FlightRecord by identifier in response to a controller query
- Remove stale FlightRecords that have timed out

Collaborators (if any):
- FlightRecord
- SafetyAnalyzer

Assumptions (if any):
- Acts as the single authoritative in-memory store; no persistent database is required for this version
- Thread-safe access is assumed when multiple subsystems read/write concurrently

Class: SafteyAnalyzer
- Periodically examine all FlightRecords to detect dangerous situations
- Detect collision risk when two aircraft are within a critical proximity threshold
- Detect altitude violations when an aircraft is outside its assigned flight level
- Detect sudden unexplained changes in speed or heading
- Generate a DangerAlert and notify RadarDisplay and ControllerQueryHandler when a hazard is found

Collaborators (if any):
- FlightRecord
- AircraftDatabse

Assumptions (if any):
- - Proximity threshold (horizontal and vertical separation minima) is configurable
- Runs on a separate analysis thread to avoid blocking the display refresh cycle
